0002: the A830 KGSL base chip-id (ROCKNIX port), Mesa 27 form.

Relations: nothing depends on it, it adds ids for a chip this stack is not
tested on (A830 / SM8750). It is kept so the stack stays what the ArmadOS
image builds: 0001-0014 on Mesa 27, and the same three image patches on
Mesa 26.2.3.

Why two files. The ROCKNIX patch was written against Mesa 26.2.3, where
`add_gpus()` for A8XX had only the base id and the KGSL id, so it added
three lines. Upstream Mesa 27 already has `GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050001,
name="Adreno (TM) 830v1")` and the KGSL `0x44050001` (as "Adreno (TM) 830"),
so the 26.2.3 hunk no longer applies and two of its three ids are a
duplicate. This file is the Mesa 27 form: the id that is still missing, the
KGSL base `0x44050000`. The old form is kept next to it as
`0002-add-a830-chip-id-mesa26.patch`, unchanged, because the image build
(`image-build/build.sh`, Mesa 26.2.3) applies that one; the rebase is
recorded in docs/mesa-27-plan.md.

Not testable here: no A830 on the bench, the A740 does not read these ids.
The change is a table row in freedreno_devices.py; the generated
freedreno_dev_info.h is what carries it into the driver.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
index a1ec052..27e20ea 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1503,6 +1503,7 @@ add_gpus([
 add_gpus([
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050000, name="Adreno (TM) 830"),
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050001, name="Adreno (TM) 830v1"),
+        GPUId(chip_id=0x44050000, name="Adreno (TM) 830"), # KGSL
         GPUId(chip_id=0x44050001, name="Adreno (TM) 830"), # KGSL
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A8XX,
